\f1 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Looking more closely at the sequence, what's striking is the order of God's actions and expectations:\
First, God reveals Himself IN Egypt: 
\f2 \uc0\u1493 \u1464 \u1488 \u1460 \u1493 \u1464 \u1468 \u1491 \u1463 \u1506 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1464 \u1492 \u1462 \u1501 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1489 \u1456 \u1468 \u1488 \u1462 \u1512 \u1462 \u1509 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1502 \u1460 \u1510 \u1456 \u1512 \u1464 \u1497 \u1460 \u1501 
\f1  - "I made myself known to them in the land of Egypt." This isn't just the burning bush to Moses; this is God making Himself known to the people while they're still in bondage.\
Then immediately (verse 7), before any deliverance, comes the command: 
\f2 \uc0\u1488 \u1460 \u1497 \u1513 \u1473 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1513 \u1460 \u1473 \u1511 \u1468 \u1493 \u1468 \u1510 \u1461 \u1497 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1506 \u1461 \u1497 \u1504 \u1464 \u1497 \u1493 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1463 \u1513 \u1456 \u1473 \u1500 \u1460 \u1497 \u1499 \u1493 \u1468 
\f1  - "each man, cast away the detestable things of his eyes." The command to abandon Egyptian idols comes BEFORE the exodus, not after. This reverses our usual understanding where God delivers first, then gives commands at Sinai.\
The phrase 
\f2 \uc0\u1513 \u1460 \u1473 \u1511 \u1468 \u1493 \u1468 \u1510 \u1461 \u1497 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1506 \u1461 \u1497 \u1504 \u1464 \u1497 \u1493 
\f1  - "detestable things of his eyes" - is peculiar. Not just "idols" but specifically what their eyes are drawn to, what they find visually compelling. This suggests the idolatry wasn't forced on them by Egyptian bondage but was their chosen visual orientation.\
The land promise includes the phrase 
\f2 \uc0\u1510 \u1456 \u1489 \u1460 \u1497 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1460 \u1497 \u1488 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1456 \u1499 \u1464 \u1500 \u1470 \u1492 \u1464 \u1488 \u1458 \u1512 \u1464 \u1510 \u1493 \u1465 \u1514 
\f1  - "it is the glory/ornament of all lands." The word 
\f2 \uc0\u1510 \u1456 \u1489 \u1460 \u1497 
\f1  connects to beauty and desire. God offers them the most desirable land while they're still fixated on the detestable things (
\f2 \uc0\u1513 \u1460 \u1473 \u1511 \u1468 \u1493 \u1468 \u1510 \u1460 \u1501 
\f1 ) their eyes desire.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <notes> The pattern emerging: - God's self-revelation precedes commands - Commands precede deliverance - They rebel even before experiencing salvation - God acts 
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1502 \u1463 \u1506 \u1463 \u1503 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1513 \u1456 \u1473 \u1502 \u1460 \u1497 
\f1  - "for my name's sake" not because they responded correctly </notes>\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Most revealing is verse 9's logic: God acts 
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1456 \u1489 \u1460 \u1500 \u1456 \u1514 \u1460 \u1468 \u1497 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1461 \u1495 \u1461 \u1500 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1456 \u1506 \u1461 \u1497 \u1504 \u1461 \u1497 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1463 \u1490 \u1468 \u1493 \u1465 \u1497 \u1460 \u1501 
\f1  - "so it wouldn't be profaned before the eyes of the nations." The nations saw God reveal Himself to Israel (
\f2 \uc0\u1488 \u1458 \u1513 \u1462 \u1473 \u1512 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1504 \u1493 \u1465 \u1491 \u1463 \u1506 \u1456 \u1514 \u1460 \u1468 \u1497 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1488 \u1458 \u1500 \u1461 \u1497 \u1492 \u1462 \u1501 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1456 \u1506 \u1461 \u1497 \u1504 \u1461 \u1497 \u1492 \u1462 \u1501 
\f1 ). Having publicly claimed Israel, God must follow through or His name would be profaned.\
This suggests the elders might think they have leverage - that God must preserve them because He's publicly committed. But God is showing them that this has ALWAYS been the only reason they survived. They've never actually sought Him properly; they've only survived because He trapped Himself in a public commitment.\
The inquiry becomes presumptuous not because they're currently idolatrous (though they are), but because they're treating God as bound to respond to them when their entire existence depends on His self-imposed obligation to His own reputation, not on any genuine relationship.
