As for the three generation pattern, recent generations of kings of Judah have prompted Ezekiel to structure previous chapters after those royal generations: 17 and 19. \
Moreover, while chapter 16 did not skip the period in the land nearly as quickly, it also focused on national origins, and the pagan tendencies of those origins. This may be the reason for the Egypt section.\
