\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 We are not told the immediate response of the elders, but I see no evidence that their silence is part of the message of this chapter. That neither elders nor people repented as a group seems clear enough from the rest of Ezekiel. For that matter, this oracle itself does not so much envision this entire generation repenting so much as needing to be purged. So while the text does not give us their immediate response, it does leave us in at least a little horror at such a rebellious people - through the lens of those who did repent, being ashamed at their past behavior.\
