Consider how the oaths sworn to their fathers in Egypt were an opportunity for partnership. As were the searching out a glorious land for them, the commands to get rid of idols, the laws that lead to life, and the Sabbaths.\
But them the people are purged of rebels. After that, the people will not just be accepted - they themselves will be a soothing aroma. Rather than offering offensive offerings to other gods, the people themselves will be an act of worship. \
Look at the pattern. Have you considered the hypothesis that the LORD will partner with his people, just not with rebellious people? And, if his people rebel, he will call out to them time and time again that they could repent and become partners. Ezekiel 18:32, "I have no pleasure in the death of anyone, declares the Lord God; so turn, and live."\
To put it another way, the LORD can plan a thing in advance, and do it by power, and yet do it through people he is in mutual relationship with, people he is partners with. If those people want to cooperate with the LORD, then there is no contradiction between those people doing what the LORD wants, and being partners.\
Look at the example of Ezekiel himself. Yes, the LORD gives exact words to say, such that he can speak the LORD's first person message. Yes, the LORD said in advance that he would make Ezekiel this kind of prophet. And yet, read the message. Ezekiel is clearly filled with the same passion the LORD is filled with. Ezekiel was given very Ezekiel shaped words. The themes, the language, even the pun in verse 29 - are these not characteristically Ezekiel? Is this not partnership, even at the same time Ezekiel is very much an instrument of God's revelation?\
Beyond this chapter, we see Ezekiel carried in the Spirit, shown both glory and wonders, even standing in God's counsel. But, perhaps most tellingly, the LORD repeatedly calls Ezekiel son of man, son of Adam, son of dirt. For Ezekiel is human, made in the image of God as Adam was, made, as all humanity was, to rule this earth, but as rulers in subjection to God.\
So yes, if people insist on evil, they are but demonstration objects. Their evil cannot stop the LORD's plans, the LORD's self revelation, the LORD's action for the sake of his name. But should they cooperate, they can be both demonstration and partners.\
